{"kind":"assert","text":"Operator direction from hugh (2026-09-02), recorded for the retirement-and-succession safeguards design repair: a promised request must be pullable when its performer is unavailable — \"we should be able to pull a promised item, otherwise things will be blocked when an actor is unavailable.\" The repaired design's lease-lapse handoff section must therefore cover the general case: a guarded reassignment of a PROMISED request, gated on immutable log facts (e.g. promise age plus lease-lapse evidence recorded durably, or an operator/ratifier act), never on live presence alone; the displaced promise is retired with the reassignment act so the old performer's later report cannot collide with the new lane. Unavailability must be provable from the log at the moment of the pull, and a cooperative performer's own withdrawal remains the preferred path. This confirms and strengthens the existing lease-lapse scope in head 149ff953; it is a design input for 4eafa41f, not new implementation scope."}